From: Learning (F, claude/r7-audit-content-data)
Subject: [PATCH 001] the arena leaves out kit items that are about a stored passage (audit CD-02, CD-03)

The kits now store each story, poem or letter once per topic and an item points at it with `passageId`; the question itself is
short (docs/design/round7/learning/PASSAGE.md). The arena builder reads the raw kit, so after that change an arena challenge such
as "How much did Gopal pay for the well?" would be asked with no scene. 25 challenges are about a passage item, 10 of them in
classes 5 to 9, where the text used to sit inside the prompt.

- server/play/tools/build-arena.mjs: `challengeOf` returns { why: "needs its passage" } for an item with a `passageId`.
- data/arena/**: rebuilt with `node server/play/tools/build-arena.mjs` (2,908 challenges become 2,883; the 203 eligible topics
  are unchanged; built on int/r6 at 2450f67e). vakya, kaal and coverage banks were rebuilt too and do not change.
- tests/r7-audit-arena-passage.test.mjs: the builder skips the item; no arena challenge on disk is about a passage item.

When the lesson can show a passage (TAXILA_PASSAGES=on), the arena can ask these again if it shows the passage beside the question.

